# Mobile patterns: Body 200 + sibling components

## Typography

Default body copy for mobile layouts and `Mobile*` components is **Body 200**:

- `font-size: var(--font-size-200)`
- `line-height: var(--line-height-200)`

Do not use desktop Body 100 (`--font-size-100`) for primary mobile reading text (messages, composer, list labels) unless Figma specifies a smaller step.

## Components

Prefer a sibling `Mobile*` component when mobile differs in type, spacing, or interaction (no hover toolbars) — same as `MobileNavigationBar` / `MobileMessageInput`. Avoid a `platform="mobile"` prop on the desktop component unless the APIs stay nearly identical.

Assume touch: no hover-revealed actions or hover row backgrounds as the primary interaction.

Desktop vs mobile choose-this-not-that, `MobileModalStage`, and home → channel motion: [src/pages/prototypes/AGENTS.md](../../src/pages/prototypes/AGENTS.md).
